The PS4 sysroot is FreeBSD 9 based: its <sys/sysctl.h> has no KERN_PROC_CWD (sysctl 42, added in
FreeBSD 10), so Boost.Process v2's cwd() for FreeBSD does not compile there. Use that branch only where
the sysctl is declared and fall back to the generic ENOTSUP version otherwise. Sunshine only includes the
v1 headers, so this merely keeps the (unused) compiled v2 library building. No change for the PS5.

--- a/libs/process/src/ext/cwd.cpp
+++ b/libs/process/src/ext/cwd.cpp
@@ -130,7 +130,7 @@
 #endif
 }
 
-#elif defined(__FreeBSD__)
+#elif defined(__FreeBSD__) && defined(KERN_PROC_CWD)
 
 filesystem::path cwd(boost::process::v2::pid_type pid, error_code & ec)
 {
